# Workers & Scheduler Rules

## Worker Registry (immutable names — update HLD + LLD before adding)

| Worker | File | Queue |
|--------|------|-------|
| `resume_parser` | `resume_parser.py` | `resume` |
| `job_scraper` | `job_scraper.py` | `scraping` |
| `job_matcher` | `job_matcher.py` | `matching` |
| `resume_optimizer` | `resume_optimizer.py` | `ai` |
| `cover_letter` | `cover_letter.py` | `ai` |
| `ats_apply` | `ats_apply.py` | `ats` |
| `recruiter_email` | `recruiter_email.py` | `email` |
| `analytics` | `analytics.py` | `analytics` |
| `notification` | `notification.py` | `notifications` |
| `cleanup` | `cleanup.py` | `maintenance` |

## Scheduler (triggers only — no business logic)

| Job | Cron | Worker Task |
|-----|------|-------------|
| Collect Jobs | Hourly | `job_scraper.collect_jobs` |
| Score Jobs | Every 30m | `job_matcher.score_all` |
| ATS Apply | 9 AM daily | `ats_apply.process_queue` |
| Recruiter Email | 10 AM daily | `recruiter_email.process_queue` |
| Analytics | Hourly | `analytics.aggregate` |
| Cleanup | Sunday 3 AM | `cleanup.run` |

## Rules

- Workers: async only, no HTTP
- Scheduler: enqueue tasks only, no scraping/AI
- Workers publish `events/` for downstream — no direct worker-to-worker calls
- Services never call `worker.delay()` — use `events/*.publish()`
